module tasks.`2026-11-23-harness-close-after-agent-cancel`

task HarnessCloseAfterAgentCancel {
  title "Find who sends the harness Close 1-14 ms before TurnEnded on an agent-side cancel; tell the delegator once when a claimed seat's agent exits"
  verify $ make test-boundaries && make test-formal
  paths "crates/bboxy450-harness", "crates/bbt-mux", "verification"
  brief """
    Our stand: subtract before you add; report what you removed.

    Follow-up to `tasks/2026-11-20-codex-seat-exits-mid-gate.den` (report `reports/2026-11-23-codex-seat-exits-mid-gate-recovery.den`).
    That task made the harness reload the same ACP session after the agent exits during recovery (harness ab591d0).
    It did not explain the incidents themselves.

    ## Evidence
    - Six cancellation logs: `SessionClosed` 5-15 ms after the failed turn; the Close op ULID was minted 1-14 ms
      BEFORE `TurnEnded` was written. kb-index: `~/.bboxy450-harness/sessions/01M82YGBZS5SH367NMA23V2AR3.jsonl:1718-1719`,
      Close cause `01M832FHVBA1Z9B5SN1FQYKD3E`. `crates/bboxy450-harness/src/backend/acp_agent.rs:819` admits `Op::Close`;
      the logs omit its caller.
    - codex-acp 2.7.0 `dist/index.js:56063` shuts down on client stdin closure; line 55177 returns Cancelled for an interrupted turn.

    ## Do
    1. Record the caller of every admitted `Op::Close` in the session log (origin field on the existing event; no new event type).
    2. Reproduce in a fresh Codex seat on the installed build with one long foreground command; find the sender from that record. Cite file:line.
    3. Make a Close that races an agent-side cancel not end a recoverable seat (or show why it must), with a process witness and a broken control.
    4. A seat whose agent exits while it holds a claimed task sends its delegator one message: last tool call and exit cause.
    5. Update the interrupt model for the Close race, with its negative control.

    ## Report from seat:01M85BY3GDQWY11RBDP8BNZESC

    Filed by the Oracle via sudo_as: this seat finished at 17:23 but lost task_report/knowledge_write after a server restart. Work: harness 9a4fe75/2973dae/971b2a4 (keep ACP recovery across terminal Close, journal process exits, keep exit evidence on interrupted reads; removes the terminal read-error fallthrough into Close) landed in harness f9f0b4a; term ad7970430/6022eb3a1/968db873b (one delegator notice per ACP agent exit with exit cause and last tool, replay fenced to claims present at exit, process witnesses gated on durable tool admission) landed as 297861f45. Oracle ran make land (formal 1001 models, native/TLC parity, clean receipt) and make test-boundaries on 297861f45: both exit 0.

    ```json
    {
      "op_id": "01M8658CAESRJMEN1ZE7VHCK1C",
      "commit": "297861f4568787f09a9eca82d13fbb288c3a4ad9",
      "report": null,
      "verify_result": {
        "command": "make test-boundaries && make test-formal",
        "exit_code": 0,
        "evidence": [
          {
            "criterion": "test-boundaries on landed source",
            "reference": "/tmp/oracle-cr-bound.log: 2+23+9 tests passed, exit 0"
          },
          {
            "criterion": "formal",
            "reference": "/tmp/oracle-close-race-land2.log: 1001 models, native/TLC parity, evidence b7701b0a6ee13bbbef06c60d167d58755291630ca1a770cf1e9b3aa9a9c39b76"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
    ```
    """

